From: emscripten-forge
Subject: wasm32: calls without JavaScript frames (JSPI), unaligned 64-bit values,
 Emscripten 4 runtime helpers

* ffi_call converts the arguments in C and calls the target through a small
  WebAssembly trampoline generated at run time, one per signature, for all
  signatures made of integers, pointers, floats and doubles.  Only
  WebAssembly frames are on the stack, so the callee may suspend with
  JavaScript Promise Integration.  Needs -sALLOW_TABLE_GROWTH; other
  signatures (structures, long double, complex, varargs) and programs
  without table growth use the JavaScript implementation as before.
  Narrow integral results are widened to ffi_arg (as upstream now does).
* The JavaScript implementation reads and writes 64-bit values through a
  DataView: HEAPF64/HEAPU64[addr >> 3] rounded addresses that are only
  4-byte aligned, which a 32-bit ABI allows and OpenJDK Zero produces
  (fix by Brian Martin, from the openjdk21 recipe).
* The JavaScript code called stackSave/stackRestore/stackAlloc and
  _malloc/_free, which Emscripten 4 only provides on request
  ("stackSave is not defined"); it now calls exported C helpers.
---
